.*
.* WRKCLS and DSPCLS: the classes of a library or the list, and the run
.* attributes one gives.
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VALCL BASETYPE='CHAR 20'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TEXTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=CLS CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=LIB CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=TEXT CLASS=TEXTCL.
:VAR NAME=RUNPTY CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=TIMESLICE CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=PURGE CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=DFTWAIT CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=CPUTIME CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=MAXTMP CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=MAXTHD CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=PADVAR CLASS=VALCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=CLASSES VARS='OPT CLS LIB TEXT'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/WRKKEYS' NAME=WRKKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display names only
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Repeat position to
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Position to
:EKEYL.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/DSPKEYS' NAME=DSPKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKCLS KEYL=WRKKEYS HELP=WRKCLS ENTER='RETURN 1'.Work with Classes
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=CLASSES ACTLEN=1 EXTACT=YES.
:LISTACT HELP='WRKCLS/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='CMD ?CRTCLS CLS(&LIB./&CLS.)'.1=Create
:LISTACT HELP='WRKCLS/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD ?CHGCLS CLS(&LIB./&CLS.)'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='WRKCLS/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DLTCLS CLS(&LIB./&CLS.)'.4=Delete
:LISTACT HELP='WRKCLS/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='CMD DSPCLS CLS(&LIB./&CLS.)'.5=Display
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKCLS/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/CLS' VAR=CLS USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Class
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/LIB' VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT EXTACT=YES.Library
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/TEXT' VAR=TEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for options 1, 2 and 5 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPCLS KEYL=DSPKEYS HELP=DSPCLS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM.Display Class Information
:DATA DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/CLS' VAR=CLS USAGE=OUTPUT.Class
:DATAGRP GRPSEP=NONE.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/LIB' VAR=LIB USAGE=OUTPUT.Library
:EDATAGRP.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/RUNPTY' VAR=RUNPTY USAGE=OUTPUT.Run priority
:DATAI HELP='FLD/TIMESLICE' VAR=TIMESLICE USAGE=OUTPUT.Time slice in milliseconds
:DATAI HELP='FLD/PURGE' VAR=PURGE USAGE=OUTPUT.Eligible for purge
:DATAI HELP='FLD/DFTWAIT' VAR=DFTWAIT USAGE=OUTPUT.Default wait time in seconds
:DATAI HELP='FLD/CPUTIME' VAR=CPUTIME USAGE=OUTPUT.Maximum CPU time in milliseconds
:DATAI HELP='FLD/MAXTMP' VAR=MAXTMP USAGE=OUTPUT.Maximum temporary storage in megabytes
:DATAI HELP='FLD/MAXTHD' VAR=MAXTHD USAGE=OUTPUT.Maximum threads
:DATAI HELP='FLD/TEXT' VAR=TEXT USAGE=OUTPUT.Text
.* Not shown: it sets the colon column.
:DATAI VAR=PADVAR USAGE=OUTPUT DISPLAY=NO.Maximum processing unit time per thread
:EDATA.
:BOTINST.Press Enter to continue.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKCLS.Work with Classes - Help
:P.The classes of the libraries asked for. Type an option next to one,
or on the first line with a new name to create one.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPCLS.Display Class Information - Help
:P.The run attributes a class gives the routing steps that use it.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F11=Display names only
:PD.Shows the list with the names alone, so more fit on a page.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Repeat position to
:PD.Repeat position to.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Positions the list at the name typed on the command line.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCLS/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CLS'.Class
:P.The class, which holds the run attributes (priority, time slice,
purge) a routing step uses.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/LIB'.Library
:P.The library of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKCLS/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it. The Create
Class (CRTCLS) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
Class (CHGCLS) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
Class (DLTCLS) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
Class (DSPCLS) command runs for the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DSPKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RUNPTY'.Run priority
:P.The run priority of the job, from 1 (highest) to 99 (lowest).
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TIMESLICE'.Time slice in milliseconds
:P.The time slice in milliseconds shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/PURGE'.Eligible for purge
:P.Whether the job may be moved out of main storage when it waits for a
long time.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/DFTWAIT'.Default wait time in seconds
:P.The default wait time in seconds shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/CPUTIME'.Maximum CPU time in milliseconds
:P.The maximum CPU time in milliseconds shown for what the display is
about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MAXTMP'.Maximum temporary storage in megabytes
:P.The maximum temporary storage in megabytes shown for what the display
is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/MAXTHD'.Maximum threads
:P.The maximum threads shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
